  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find the $x$-coordinates of any points on $y=(4x-7)^3$ where the tangent is:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Parallel to $y=108x+7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac52$ or $x=1$.",
          "worked": "The required tangent gradient is $108$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=3(4x-7)^2(4)\\\\&=12(4x-7)^2\\\\12(4x-7)^2&=108\\\\(4x-7)^2&=9\\\\4x-7&=\\pm3\\\\x&=\\frac52\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Perpendicular to $x+12y+6=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$ or $x=\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}12y&=-x-6\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe given line has gradient $-\\frac1{12}$, so the required tangent gradient is $12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=3(4x-7)^2(4)\\\\&=12(4x-7)^2\\\\12(4x-7)^2&=12\\\\(4x-7)^2&=1\\\\4x-7&=\\pm1\\\\x&=2\\text{ or }\\frac32\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      }
    ]
  },
